### TeamForge Phase 2 API Tests (REST Client Format)
### Appeals and Reports: User Reporting, Admin Review, Actions, Warnings Appeals, and Audit Filter

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@adminToken = Bearer YOUR_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE
@collaboratorToken = Bearer YOUR_COLLABORATOR_TOKEN_HERE
@targetUserId = 4
@warningId = YOUR_ACTIVE_WARNING_ID_HERE
@reportId = YOUR_REPORT_ID_HERE
@appealId = YOUR_APPEAL_ID_HERE

### 1. Search Users for Reporting (Success - Safe Public Fields Only)
# Expected Status: 200 OK
# Expected Response: Array of [{ id, name, username, university }] (Never email or private fields)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/search?q=ro
Authorization: {{collaboratorToken}}

###

### 2. Search Users - Query < 2 Characters
# Expected Status: 200 OK
# Expected Response: []
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/search?q=r
Authorization: {{collaboratorToken}}

###

### 3. Submit Report Against User (Success)
# Expected Status: 201 Created
# Expected Response: { id, reporterId, reportedUserId, reason, details, status: "Open", ... }
POST {{baseUrl}}/reports
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{collaboratorToken}}

{
  "reportedUserId": "{{targetUserId}}",
  "reason": "Harassment",
  "details": "User has repeatedly posted derogatory messages in the project channels."
}

###

### 4. Submit Report - Cannot Report Self
# Expected Status: 403 Forbidden
# Expected Response: { "statusCode": 403, "error": "Forbidden", "code": "CANNOT_REPORT_SELF", "message": "You cannot report your own account." }
POST {{baseUrl}}/reports
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{collaboratorToken}}

{
  "reportedUserId": "2",
  "reason": "Spam",
  "details": "Testing self reporting prevention guard."
}

###

### 5. Submit Report - Cannot Report Admin
# Expected Status: 403 Forbidden
# Expected Response: { "statusCode": 403, "error": "Forbidden", "code": "CANNOT_REPORT_ADMIN", "message": "You cannot report an administrator or superuser account." }
POST {{baseUrl}}/reports
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{collaboratorToken}}

{
  "reportedUserId": "1",
  "reason": "Spam",
  "details": "Attempting to report platform administrator."
}

###

### 6. Submit Report - Duplicate Open Report Conflict
# Expected Status: 409 Conflict
# Expected Response: { "statusCode": 409, "error": "Conflict", "code": "DUPLICATE_OPEN_REPORT", "message": "You already have an open report pending review against this user." }
POST {{baseUrl}}/reports
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{collaboratorToken}}

{
  "reportedUserId": "{{targetUserId}}",
  "reason": "Spam",
  "details": "Second open report while first report is still pending review."
}

###

### 7. Get Current User Submitted Reports (Outcome Line Only)
# Expected Status: 200 OK
# Expected Response: Array of own reports with status and outcome summary
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/mine
Authorization: {{collaboratorToken}}

###

### 8. Admin List Reports (Filtered & Paginated)
# Expected Status: 200 OK (Requires "reports" permission)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/reports?status=Open&page=1&limit=10
Authorization: {{adminToken}}

###

### 9. Admin Get Report Details (With Earlier Warnings & Reports)
# Expected Status: 200 OK
# Expected Response: Full details, reporter, reported user, earlier warnings, earlier reports
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/reports/{{reportId}}
Authorization: {{adminToken}}

###

### 10. Admin Update Report Status
# Expected Status: 200 OK
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/reports/{{reportId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{adminToken}}

{
  "status": "Under review",
  "note": "Investigation opened by admin."
}

###

### 11. Admin Action on Report (Warn Action)
# Expected Status: 201 Created
# Expected Response: Resolves report, issues warning via Phase 1 ModerationService, notifies reporter
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/reports/{{reportId}}/action
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{adminToken}}

{
  "action": "warn",
  "reason": "Official warning issued for community guidelines breach."
}

###

### 12. Submit Appeal for Active Warning (Success)
# Expected Status: 201 Created
# Expected Response: { id, warningId, userId, explanation, status: "pending", ... }
POST {{baseUrl}}/warnings/{{warningId}}/appeal
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{collaboratorToken}}

{
  "explanation": "I had an unexpected power outage and posted notice in Discord as soon as power returned."
}

###

### 13. Submit Appeal - Already Appealed Conflict
# Expected Status: 409 Conflict
# Expected Response: { "statusCode": 409, "error": "Conflict", "code": "ALREADY_APPEALED", "message": "This warning has already been appealed. Only one appeal is permitted per warning." }
POST {{baseUrl}}/warnings/{{warningId}}/appeal
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{collaboratorToken}}

{
  "explanation": "Second appeal attempt for the exact same warning."
}

###

### 14. Get Current User Appeals
# Expected Status: 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me/appeals
Authorization: {{collaboratorToken}}

###

### 15. Admin List Appeals
# Expected Status: 200 OK (Requires "reports" permission)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/appeals?status=pending
Authorization: {{adminToken}}

###

### 16. Admin Decide on Appeal (Accept Decision)
# Expected Status: 201 Created
# Expected Response: Appeal accepted, warning removed, +10 reputation restored once, active count lowered
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/appeals/{{appealId}}/decision
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{adminToken}}

{
  "decision": "accept",
  "note": "Documentation reviewed and confirmed. Warning removed from record."
}

###

### 17. Admin Audit Log Filtered by User ID
# Expected Status: 200 OK
# Expected Response: Audit log entries where actor or target matches the specified user ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/audit?userId={{targetUserId}}
Authorization: {{adminToken}}
